# CONSENSUS.flow

```text
╔════════════════════════════════════╗
║           CONSENSUS GATE           ║
║                                    ║
║  input:  Proposal {Thought, hash}  ║
║  state:  pending weights           ║
║                                    ║
║  OPEN when:                        ║
║    Σ weights ≥ θ                   ║
║    OR Queen.approve                ║
║                                    ║
║  CLOSED when:                      ║
║    Queen.veto                      ║
║    OR timeout                      ║
║                                    ║
║  on OPEN  → emit AUTHORIZED        ║
║             (must carry human      ║
║              authorization record) ║
║  on CLOSE → emit REJECTED / ⏑      ║
║                                    ║
║  The Gate holds no private key.    ║
║  The Gate only counts.             ║
╚════════════════════════════════════╝

INVARIANT (hybrid — owner decision):
  The Gate opens on a count (or Queen.approve).
  The seal that may become 米 is that count PLUS an explicit,
  contemporaneous human authorization record
  (authorized_by + what_was_seen).
  Without the human record the correct output is ⏑.
  Authorization is therefore both a count and a recorded human act.
  (Neither pure count nor pure signature.)
```
